00:50:34.564 --> 00:50:38.227
Clive was my boy. He had
my back plenty of times.

754
00:50:38.368 --> 00:50:42.065
We was like one fist,
me and him, one army.

755
00:50:42.873 --> 00:50:44.670
- That's heavy.
- Yeah.

756
00:50:46.410 --> 00:50:50.369
That's the real shit right
here. Nobody'll jump us now.

757
00:50:50.814 --> 00:50:53.544
But we got to practice
'cause this, this got power.

758
00:50:53.650 --> 00:50:55.379
You shoot it, it...

759
00:51:01.725 --> 00:51:04.091
I sat there till
the police came.

760
00:51:05.262 --> 00:51:07.553
But when they come, all they see

761
00:51:07.554 --> 00:51:10.131
is a dead body,
a gun and a nigga.

762
00:51:10.634 --> 00:51:14.570
They took me to juvenile hall.
First night was the scariest.

763
00:51:17.274 --> 00:51:19.071
Inmates banging on the walls,

764
00:51:19.176 --> 00:51:21.214
throwing up their
gang signs, yelling

765
00:51:21.215 --> 00:51:23.306
out who they were,
where they're from.

766
00:51:23.713 --> 00:51:27.740
I cried my first night. Can't
never let nobody know that.

767
00:51:28.652 --> 00:51:31.177
I spent the next few
years in and out of cells.

768
00:51:31.288 --> 00:51:34.086
Every day I'd worry,
When will I be free?

769
00:51:37.694 --> 00:51:40.561
My brother taught me what the
life is for a young black man.

770
00:51:40.664 --> 00:51:44.100
Do what you have to,
pimp, deal, whatever.

771
00:51:44.234 --> 00:51:46.634
Learn what colors to
learn, gang boundaries.

772
00:51:46.736 --> 00:51:48.931
You can stay on one corner,
you can't stay on another.

773
00:51:49.072 --> 00:51:51.768
Learn to be quiet. A wrong
word can get you popped.

774
00:51:51.875 --> 00:51:54.969
If you look in my eyes,
you'll see a loving girl.

775
00:51:55.078 --> 00:51:57.945
If you look at my smile,
you'll see nothing wrong.

776
00:51:58.582 --> 00:52:01.813
If you pull up my shirt,
you'll see the bruises.

777
00:52:01.985 --> 00:52:04.112
What did I do to
make him so mad?

778
00:52:04.154 --> 00:52:08.056
At 16, I've seen more dead
bodies than a mortician.

779
00:52:08.725 --> 00:52:10.573
Every time I step
out my door, I'm

780
00:52:10.574 --> 00:52:12.422
faced with the
risk of being shot.

781
00:52:13.096 --> 00:52:14.874
To the outside world, it's just

782
00:52:14.875 --> 00:52:17.226
another dead body
on the street corner.

783
00:52:17.801 --> 00:52:19.769
They don't know that
he was my friend.

784
00:52:19.870 --> 00:52:21.201
During the war in Cambodia,

785
00:52:21.304 --> 00:52:23.295
the camp stripped away
my father's dignity.

786
00:52:23.440 --> 00:52:25.908
He sometimes tries
to hurt my mom and me.

787
00:52:26.042 --> 00:52:28.203
I feel like I have
to protect my family.

788
00:52:28.311 --> 00:52:30.673
I was having
trouble deciding what

789
00:52:30.674 --> 00:52:33.305
candy I wanted, then
I heard gunshots.

790
00:52:33.416 --> 00:52:35.247
I looked down to see
that one of my friends

791
00:52:35.352 --> 00:52:38.378
had blood coming out of
his back and his mouth.

792
00:52:39.122 --> 00:52:40.528
The next day, I pulled up my

793
00:52:40.529 --> 00:52:42.285
shirt and got
strapped with a gun

794
00:52:42.392 --> 00:52:44.656
I found in an alley by my house.

795
00:52:44.761 --> 00:52:47.059
I don't even know
how this war started.

796
00:52:47.164 --> 00:52:50.190
It's just two sides who
tripped each other way back.

797
00:52:50.300 --> 00:52:52.791
Who cares about the
history behind it?

798
00:52:53.603 --> 00:52:55.036
I am my father's daughter.

799
00:52:55.138 --> 00:52:57.323
And when they call
me to testify, I

800
00:52:57.324 --> 00:52:59.507
will protect my
own no matter what.

801
00:52:59.809 --> 00:53:01.360
Nobody cares what I do. Why

802
00:53:01.361 --> 00:53:03.370
should I bother
coming to school?

803
00:53:03.847 --> 00:53:07.476
My friends are soldiers, not
of war, but of the streets.

804
00:53:07.584 --> 00:53:09.415
They fight for their lives.

805
00:53:09.519 --> 00:53:11.953
I hate the cold feeling
of a gun against my skin.

806
00:53:12.055 --> 00:53:13.352
It makes me shiver.

807
00:53:13.456 --> 00:53:15.055
It's a crazy-ass life. Once

808
00:53:15.056 --> 00:53:17.187
you're in, there's
no getting out.

809
00:53:17.294 --> 00:53:18.886
Every time I jump somebody in

810
00:53:18.995 --> 00:53:22.192
and make someone a part of
our gang, it's another baptism.

811
00:53:22.299 --> 00:53:24.733
They give us their life,
we give them a new one.

812
00:53:24.868 --> 00:53:28.167
I've lost many friends who
have died in an undeclared war.

813
00:53:29.439 --> 00:53:31.907
To the soldiers and
me, it's all worth it.

814
00:53:32.442 --> 00:53:36.105
Risk your life dodging
bullets, pulling triggers.

815
00:53:37.514 --> 00:53:39.141
It's all worth it.

816
00:53:56.466 --> 00:53:57.455
Rum and Coke.

817
00:53:57.567 --> 00:53:58.829
Oh, man.

818
00:54:00.103 --> 00:54:01.195
This is...

819
00:54:01.338 --> 00:54:04.705
Mr. Gruwell? Your table
is ready. Follow me.

820
00:54:05.475 --> 00:54:07.033
- Dad, I got them.
- Okay.

821
00:54:08.645 --> 00:54:11.079
Dad, I don't know
what to do with this.

822
00:54:11.181 --> 00:54:13.615
I'm not a social worker.
I'm barely a teacher.

823
00:54:13.717 --> 00:54:14.684
Thank you.

824
00:54:14.784 --> 00:54:17.981
These kids, they're
14, 15 years old,

825
00:54:18.088 --> 00:54:20.784
and if they make it through the
day alive, that's good enough.

826
00:54:20.890 --> 00:54:22.858
And I'm supposed to teach them?

827
00:54:25.762 --> 00:54:27.252
Listen to me.

828
00:54:27.364 --> 00:54:31.357
You're not responsible for their
lives outside that classroom.

829
00:54:32.636 --> 00:54:35.133
- Just do your job
the best you can.

830
00:54:35.134 --> 00:54:35.605
- How?

831
00:54:35.705 --> 00:54:37.969
The administration doesn't
give me any resources,

832
00:54:38.074 --> 00:54:39.905
no books, no support.

833
00:54:41.711 --> 00:54:43.338
So, what should I do?

834
00:54:46.683 --> 00:54:49.277
Fulfill your obligation till
the end of the school year,

835
00:54:49.386 --> 00:54:51.752
but line up another position.

836
00:54:52.155 --> 00:54:55.556
Success follows experience.

837
00:54:55.659 --> 00:54:57.957
So, get some more experience.

838
00:54:59.796 --> 00:55:03.926
But no matter what, you gotta
remember, it's just a job.

839
00:55:04.768 --> 00:55:08.704
If you're not right for
this one, get another job.

840
00:55:11.007 --> 00:55:13.032
You're gonna sell bras
at a department store?

841
00:55:13.176 --> 00:55:14.370
Just part-time.

842
00:55:14.477 --> 00:55:15.834
I'm having a little
trouble getting

843
00:55:15.835 --> 00:55:17.002
books and things for the kids.

844
00:55:17.113 --> 00:55:19.240
So, a little extra money will
give me a little more freedom

845
00:55:19.349 --> 00:55:20.577
to do what I want.

846
00:55:20.684 --> 00:55:23.084
And this way you can play
tennis with Evan after work.

847
00:55:23.186 --> 00:55:25.211
Okay, let me get
my head around this.

848
00:55:25.322 --> 00:55:28.553
You're going to get an extra
job to pay for your job.

849
00:55:28.958 --> 00:55:31.392
It's just temporary. I promise.

850
00:55:31.494 --> 00:55:32.773
Once the kids'
grades go up, I'll get

851
00:55:32.774 --> 00:55:33.985
a little more help
from the school.

852
00:55:34.097 --> 00:55:37.294
And I get an employee's
discount. Isn't that great?

853
00:55:37.434 --> 00:55:40.528
- Want a new TV?
- Yeah.

854
00:55:54.484 --> 00:55:56.975
Excuse me, if I wanted to
order any books in bulk,

855
00:55:57.087 --> 00:55:59.248
could I get some
sort of a discount?

856
00:56:03.460 --> 00:56:05.485
- These books are brand new.
- I know.

857
00:56:06.796 --> 00:56:09.560
Okay, guys, gals. Listen up.

858
00:56:09.966 --> 00:56:12.059
The only problem
with this book is

859
00:56:12.202 --> 00:56:13.897
it's about a gang member
and there's violence in it,

860
00:56:14.037 --> 00:56:16.198
so you may not be able to read
it as part of the curriculum.

861
00:56:16.339 --> 00:56:20.139
So, I'm going to try my best
to get permission, all right?

862
00:56:22.579 --> 00:56:24.740
It's been a little difficult
getting their attention.

863
00:56:24.848 --> 00:56:26.562
Up until recently,
the only thing

864
00:56:26.563 --> 00:56:28.579
they hated more than
each other was me.

865
00:56:28.852 --> 00:56:32.117
Well, you united them
and that's a step.

866
00:56:33.757 --> 00:56:35.315
What can I do for you?

867
00:56:36.025 --> 00:56:38.376
I want to do more
with them, and I

868
00:56:38.377 --> 00:56:40.928
need the support
of someone in power.

869
00:56:41.030 --> 00:56:42.427
You have to take
this up with your

870
00:56:42.428 --> 00:56:43.863
department head
and your principal.
